WEBVTT

seg-1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.300
<v Alice Andersson>Welcome everyone to the architecture review for the regional network.</v>

seg-2
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:08.800
<v Alice Andersson>This is revision A of the network architecture document.</v>

seg-3
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:16.800
<v Alice Andersson>Here is the agenda for today, we will end with decisions.</v>

seg-4
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:22.800
<v Alice Andersson>As you see here, the new edge data centre in Karlskrona sits between aggregation and core.</v>

seg-5
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:28.800
<v Bob Berg>The access rings are still single-homed, which is the main availability risk.</v>

seg-6
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:37.800
<v Alice Andersson>Our design principles: automate everything that is repeated and go dual-homed.</v>

seg-7
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:46.800
<v Bob Berg>The latency budget is five milliseconds end to end, timing comes from PTP grandmasters.</v>

seg-8
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:55.800
<v Alice Andersson>The 5G core user plane moves to the edge, the control plane stays central.</v>

seg-9
00:00:56.200 --> 00:01:03.800
<v Bob Berg>We migrate in three phases, starting with lab validation.</v>

seg-10
00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:09.800
<v Alice Andersson>Decision: we adopt dual-homed aggregation for all regions.</v>

seg-11
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.800
<v Alice Andersson>Action item: Bob validates the lab results by June.</v>

seg-12
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.800
<v Bob Berg>The biggest risk is vendor lead time for 100G optics.</v>

seg-13
00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:25.800
<v Alice Andersson>Thanks all, the recording and slides will be shared on the site.</v>
